{"title":"1978 USAMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Problems from the <b>1978 <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=United_States_of_America_Mathematical_Olympiad\" title=\"United States of America Mathematical Olympiad\"> USAMO</a></b>.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/5/5753734e29398cf1e59cb67a78e86180c7499f2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c,d,e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" /> are real numbers such that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/f/05f467267dead70564508abb27cff6b8ffe78120.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c+d+e=8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"165\" height=\"14\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/5/b8553245a133c0cdb1dcb4ee3bfdc717065177d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2+c^2+d^2+e^2=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"211\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Determine the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3a59bb1293ee3f6dec19de4019a7178874219ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1978 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/a/d4aa4d85335863f762ae4128b05ede6d4e918678.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;B&#39;C&#39;D&#39;$\" width=\"75\" height=\"14\" /> are square maps of the same region, drawn to different scales and superimposed as shown in the figure. Prove that there is only one point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> on the small map that lies directly over point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f2d56588b9482ec9e17dc73757691f883f6cee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> of the large map such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f2d56588b9482ec9e17dc73757691f883f6cee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O&#39;$\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> each represent the same place of the country. Also, give a Euclidean construction (straight edge and compass) for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/a/6fa08871047fa32076357c574b19dfeb124210b6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] defaultpen(linewidth(0.7)+fontsize(10)); real theta = -100, r = 0.3; pair D2 = (0.3,0.76); string[] lbl = {&#39;A&#39;, &#39;B&#39;, &#39;C&#39;, &#39;D&#39;}; draw(unitsquare); draw(shift(D2)*rotate(theta)*scale(r)*unitsquare); for(int i = 0; i &lt; lbl.length; ++i) { pair Q = dir(135-90*i), P = (.5,.5)+Q/2^.5; label(&quot;$&quot;+lbl[i]+&quot;&#39;$&quot;, P, Q); label(&quot;$&quot;+lbl[i]+&quot;$&quot;,D2+rotate(theta)*(r*P), rotate(theta)*Q); }[/asy]\" width=\"668\" height=\"655\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1978 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> will be called <i>good</i> if we can write\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/a/e6addc40361b4725dbb976f67e392cd2f8f4d94e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=a_1+a_2+\\cdots+a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"173\" height=\"13\" />,\n</p><p>where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/c/6fc08f1e2692facb3caf6f6e9a13178c8615bc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1,a_2, \\ldots, a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"99\" height=\"11\" /> are positive integers (not necessarily distinct) satisfying\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/acc69aeaf9edf2e55478934554af19e5b38caf52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{a_1}+\\frac{1}{a_2}+\\cdots+\\frac{1}{a_k}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"187\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>Given the information that the integers 33 through 73 are good, prove that every integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/6/84648e41ee24543af758bb1d4d3c34b8933d371d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ge 33$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"39\" height=\"16\" /> is good.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1978 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(a) Prove that if the six dihedral (i.e. angles between pairs of faces) of a given tetrahedron are congruent, then the tetrahedron is regular.\n</p><p>(b) Is a tetrahedron necessarily regular if five dihedral angles are congruent?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1978 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Nine mathematicians meet at an international conference and discover that among any three of them, at least two speak a common language. If each of the mathematicians speak at most three languages, prove that there are at least three of the mathematicians who can speak the same language.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1978 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_USAMO\" title=\"1978 USAMO\">1978 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1978\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1977_USAMO\" title=\"1977 USAMO\">1977 USAMO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1979_USAMO\" title=\"1979 USAMO\">1979 USAMO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1978 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1978 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1978 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1978 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1978_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1978 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017195408\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.029 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.049 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 137/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1209/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 60/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnst